.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-singleton-detach 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-singleton\-detach \- Run a command in the background under a task\*(Aqs lock, and report the previous run\*(Aqs failure
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten singleton detach\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-marker\fR> <\fB\-\-log\fR> <\fB\-\-pattern\fR> <\fItask\fR> <\fIcommand\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a command in the background under a task\*(Aqs lock, and report the previous run\*(Aqs failure
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-marker\fR \fI<marker>\fR
Where a failed run\*(Aqs pointers wait, announced and cleared by the next invocation
.TP
\fB\-\-log\fR \fI<log>\fR
Where the background run\*(Aqs whole output is written
.TP
\fB\-\-pattern\fR \fI<pattern>\fR
The `[[pattern]]` row whose matching output lines are the failure\*(Aqs pointers
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fItask\fR>
The task\*(Aqs name, which is what the lock is keyed by
.TP
<\fIcommand\fR>
The command to run in the background, after `\-\-`
